---
import FallCourseLayout from '../../../layouts/FallCourseLayout.astro';
import { fall, displayDate } from '../../../lib/fall2026';
---
<FallCourseLayout title="Assignments">
  <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/1/">Course</a> / Assignments</p><h1>Build a body of work.</h1><p class="page-intro">Small source experiments support the projects. Each finished project becomes part of the portfolio.</p>
  {fall.grading.map(group=><section><h2>{group.label} <span class="muted">{group.weight}%</span></h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Work</th><th>Due</th><th>Points</th></tr></thead><tbody>{fall.assignments.filter(a=>a.group===group.id).map(a=><tr><td><a href={`/1/assignments/${a.id}/`}>{a.title}</a></td><td>{displayDate(a.dueDate)}</td><td>{a.points}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>)}
  <div class="callout"><p>Category weights determine the final grade. Weekly evidence evaluates your practice; projects evaluate the finished page; the final portfolio evaluates curation, navigation, and presentation. The same work is not graded twice for the same criteria.</p><a href="/1/resources/rubrics/">Read the assessment criteria</a></div>
</FallCourseLayout>
